From 4008a8d84896c1b22a8a523ee0524bb4ae3bfcf9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:09:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CoCoXSID: an emulated SID sound cartridge

New cart type 'cocoxsid': SID register n at $FF40+n (the SCS window, so it
sits in a Multi-Pak slot selected through $FF7F), driven by src/sid.c, a
compact 6581 emulation: three voices with triangle/saw/pulse/noise and ANDed
combinations, ADSR envelopes, ring modulation, hard sync, the state-variable
filter, and OSC3/ENV3 readback.  The chip runs at an assumed 1.000 MHz clock
(the published player's pitch table is tuned to it).  Its audio goes through
the sound interface's non-muxed (external) input, like the real board's Ext
jack.

tools/sid_test.c checks the core against the data sheet: pitch, pulse width,
attack times, sustain, release, volume, filters, sync, readable registers.
